In article <1993Sep3.184247.4084@twg.com>, blume@twg.com (David Blume) writes:
> Has anyone completed the priest quest when their priest was neutral?  If so,
> what did you do to protect yourself from level-draining?
> 
Spoilers!






1) Wear one of the following pieces of armor:
   - mithril-coat (any type)
   - cloak of protection
   - cloak of magic resistance
   - elven cloak
   - oilskin cloak
   This will make you almost immune to level drains (~1% chance of draining
   per successful attack).
2) Deal with few undead at a time (best with just one...) To achieve this
   just use the fact that undead will follow you upstairs. Go level down,
   wait till one-two approach, go up, finish them, repeat.

Imanaged this way to do the priest quest without a single level drain
- which didn't protect me from being killed by the quest bad guy :-(

